<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Said Ali bin Said Omar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Said Ali of Bambao</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Said Ali bin Said Omar was sultan of Bambao on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grande-comore">Grande Comore</a> (Ngazidja) in the late 19th century. Backed by the French adventurer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leon-humblot">Léon Humblot</a>, he made himself paramount sultan of the island and in 1886 signed a treaty placing all of Grande Comore under a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>. The treaty ended the independence of the island's rival sultanates, including Itsandra, and opened the way to French rule over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comoro-islands">Comoros</a>.</p></div>
